# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
# NOT anchored with a leading slash — must match testbed/, apps/, packages/ too.
# A leading-slash rule silently let testbed/node_modules (520MB) through.
node_modules/
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env*.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# build output (any workspace)
dist/
/out/

# logs
*.log

# local scratch — never commit
scratch/
tmp/

# Evidence we DO commit, stated explicitly so nobody "tidies" it away:
#   data/scan-runs/**    timestamped raw scan results = the evidence trail
#   *_sponsor.md         sponsor prize terms, for reference
#   preflight-brief-*.md, ROADMAP.md, rules.md, IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
#     spec + planning artifacts — ETHGlobal REQUIRES these in the repo when a
#     spec-driven workflow is used (see competition.md / ETHICS.md §7)
